    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="search-hit">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2510.00174v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        As the adoption of language <span class="search-hit mathjax">models</span> advances, so does the need to better represent individual users to the&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2510.00174v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2510.00174v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2510.00174v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        As the adoption of language <span class="search-hit mathjax">models</span> advances, so does the need to better represent individual users to the <span class="search-hit mathjax">model</span>. Are there aspects of an individual&#39;s belief system that a language <span class="search-hit mathjax">model</span> can utilize for improved alignment? Following prior research, we investigate this question in the domain of opinion prediction by developing PrimeX, a dataset of public opinion survey data from 858 US residents with two additional sources of belief information: written explanations from the respondents for why they hold specific opinions, and the Primal <span class="search-hit mathjax">World</span> Belief survey for assessing respondent worldview. We provide an extensive initial analysis of our data and show the value of belief explanations and worldview for personalizing language <span class="search-hit mathjax">models</span>. Our results demonstrate how the additional belief information in PrimeX can benefit both the NLP and psychological research communities, opening up avenues for further study.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2510.00174v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2510.00174v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
